<body>
<div class="Section1">

  <!-- PAGE 1 -->
  <h1 class="chapter-title">Chapter 1: Introduction</h1>
  
  <h2 class="section-title">1.1 Introduction</h2>
  <p>
    In contemporary daily living, domestic maintenance and utility services—such as plumbing, electrical repairs, home appliance servicing, carpentry, and deep cleaning—are essential for maintaining household infrastructure and residential living standards. However, the domestic home services market has historically remained unorganized, fragmented, and heavily dependent on informal communication. At the same time, households face considerable challenges in identifying reliable, skilled, and punctual service professionals. In many cases, independent technicians operate without standard pricing or verified credentials, resulting in mistrust and uncertainty between households and technicians. Therefore, there is a distinct need for an organized system through which essential domestic services can be discovered, scheduled, monitored, and evaluated.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Web Development Project titled <strong>“ServiGo: An On-Demand Local Services Marketplace and Discovery Platform”</strong> focuses on developing a web-based solution to address this issue. The proposed platform aims to connect consumers seeking domestic repairs with skilled local service providers, tradespeople, and specialized technicians. According to the project specifications, service providers can provide information regarding their trade, services, hourly rates, location, and availability. Customers can identify and book suitable technicians, while platform administrators oversee service standards and provider verification.
  </p>
  <p>
    The project combines community participation with modern full-stack web engineering to create a more systematic approach to domestic service delivery. Instead of depending entirely on informal recommendations, the proposed platform provides a centralized system for managing service appointments and coordinating participants. Features such as service category navigation, location-based search, notifications, booking status tracking, and provider ratings help improve the overall hiring experience.
  </p>

  <h2 class="section-title">1.2 Purpose of the Project</h2>
  <p>
    The main purpose of this Web Development Project is to explore how a technology-based marketplace can help organize local domestic services and facilitate transparent, convenient service transactions within communities. The project seeks to provide a structured method for connecting household consumers with verified service professionals.
  </p>
  <div class="page-footer">1</div>

  <br class="page-break" style="page-break-before:always;" />

  <!-- PAGE 2 -->
  <p>
    The platform is intended to make the process of booking local technicians more convenient and organized. A service provider can enter relevant information about their skills, pricing, and service coverage, allowing households to identify service options according to their requirements and location. The integrated communication and booking modules further support this coordination by enabling direct coordination of visit schedules, addresses, and service requirements.
  </p>

  <h2 class="section-title">1.3 Objectives of the Project</h2>
  <p>
    The major objectives of the <strong>ServiGo Local Services Marketplace Platform</strong> are as follows:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>To develop a web-based platform for managing and coordinating local domestic service requests.</li>
    <li>To connect households and commercial clients with verified service providers across essential categories such as Plumbing, Electrical, Appliance Repair, Carpentry, and Cleaning.</li>
    <li>To provide service professionals with an accessible method of listing their skills, services, and pricing.</li>
    <li>To enable customers to search, compare, and book suitable service providers based on specialization, pricing, customer reviews, and geographic location.</li>
    <li>To support direct real-time communication between customers and service providers through integrated in-app messaging.</li>
    <li>To provide an interactive, location-based map interface for visualizing nearby service professionals and improving service reach.</li>
    <li>To maintain complete digital records of service requests and their progress through an automated booking status tracking workflow.</li>
    <li>To establish a community-driven reputation and quality assurance mechanism through star ratings and verified customer reviews.</li>
    <li>To provide an administrative dashboard for managing users, service categories, provider verification badges, and reports.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 class="section-title">1.4 Background Information</h2>
  <p>
    Accessing reliable domestic services is not only a matter of personal convenience but also represents household safety, appliance longevity, and domestic resource management. When domestic repairs are delayed or executed by unqualified individuals, households face property damage and excessive expenditures. Community-based service discovery can therefore play an important role in organizing local labor resources and improving service dependability.
  </p>
  <div class="page-footer">2</div>

  <br class="page-break" style="page-break-before:always;" />

  <!-- PAGE 3 -->
  <p>
    The proposed project considers the different participants involved in the domestic services ecosystem: household consumers seeking prompt domestic repairs, independent tradespeople offering maintenance services, and platform administrators supervising system compliance and trust verification.
  </p>

  <div class="flowchart-container">
    <div class="flow-box">User Roles: Customer / Provider / Admin</div><br>
    ↓<br>
    <div class="flow-box">React 19 Frontend (Vite + Bootstrap 5 + Leaflet Map)</div><br>
    ↓<br>
    <div class="flow-box">[JWT Auth &amp; bcryptjs] ↔ [REST API: Express.js] ↔ [Socket.io Real-Time Engine]</div><br>
    ↓<br>
    <div class="flow-box">Prisma ORM (Schema &amp; Relation Layer)</div><br>
    ↓<br>
    <div class="flow-box">SQLite Relational Database (dev.db)</div>
  </div>
  <div class="figure-caption">Figure 1.1: System Architecture and Technology Stack Relationship</div>

  <table class="report-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 22%;">System Layer</th>
