        <td>Customer submits 1-5 star rating and feedback; updates provider public score.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p>
    The proposed <strong>ServiGo Local Services Marketplace Platform</strong> builds on these ideas by bringing different participants together on a single web-based platform. The project connects household consumers with skilled service providers across essential domestic trades.
  </p>
  <div class="page-footer">5</div>

  <br class="page-break" style="page-break-before:always;" />

  <!-- PAGE 6 -->
  <h1 class="chapter-title">Chapter 3: Methodology</h1>
  <p>
    The methodology of the project focuses on understanding the operational challenges of the local domestic services sector and studying how service seekers can be effectively connected with skilled local providers. The project uses observational methods, informal discussions, interviews, and secondary research to understand the existing service procurement process and identify the requirements for the proposed <strong>ServiGo Local Services Marketplace Platform</strong>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Observation was used to understand how domestic maintenance requests are generated, scheduled, and resolved in the community. The process of finding technicians and the challenges involved in identifying available workers, price negotiation, and reliability were considered. Attention was given to factors such as the availability of skilled workers, communication between participants, travel logistics, and timely completion of work.
  </p>
  <p>
    Discussions with people involved in hiring domestic help and independent technicians provided information about how customers currently search for help, how technicians acquire work leads, and how both parties coordinate timing and pricing.
  </p>
  <p>
    Secondary research was also used to gather information related to the gig-economy, domestic services, platform trust mechanisms, and the use of technology in local market organization. Online articles, reports, research papers, and other relevant sources help provide background information and an understanding of existing approaches to local service discovery.
  </p>
  <p>
    The main tools used for data collection include observation notes, interview questions, informal discussions, online research, and documentation of relevant information. These methods were selected because the project addresses a real community problem and requires an understanding of the experiences and requirements of different stakeholders. Observation provides practical understanding, interviews and discussions provide direct viewpoints, and secondary research provides supporting background information.
  </p>
  <p>
    The information collected through these methods helps identify the requirements of the proposed platform. Based on these findings, features such as category-based browsing, location-based map search, notifications, booking tracking, and in-app chat can be included in the system. The proposed platform aims to connect households with verified service providers to make domestic service discovery and delivery more organized and efficient.
  </p>
  <div class="page-footer">6</div>

  <br class="page-break" style="page-break-before:always;" />

  <!-- PAGE 7 -->
  <h1 class="chapter-title">Chapter 4: Description, Observation and Analysis</h1>
  
  <p>
    <span class="bold-label">Description:</span><br>
    The project team interacted with community members and local service providers to understand the problem of unorganized home services and the process of finding local technicians. The interactions focused on household consumers, independent technicians (such as plumbers and electricians), and the challenges involved in scheduling, price transparency, and skill verification.
  </p>

  <div class="flowchart-container">
    <div class="flow-box">[User (Customer/Provider/Admin)] → [ProviderProfile (Bio, City, Rate)] → [Category &amp; Services]</div><br>
    ↓<br>
    <div class="flow-box">[Location Coordinates (Map Pin)] → [Booking (Status, Date, Address)] → [Review (1-5 Stars)]</div><br>
    ↓<br>
    <div class="flow-box">[Conversation (Customer + Provider)] ↔ [Messages (Real-time Socket.io Stream)]</div>
  </div>
  <div class="figure-caption">Figure 4.1: Database Relationship and Entity Association Overview</div>

  <p>
    <span class="bold-label">Observation:</span><br>
    It was observed that domestic service requests often suffer from delays and misunderstandings due to a lack of proper communication, transparent pricing, and coordination. Independent technicians struggle to secure consistent work orders, while households face difficulties verifying the credibility of unknown workers entering their homes.
  </p>

  <p>
    <span class="bold-label">Analysis:</span><br>
    The information collected was analyzed according to the objectives of the project. The findings showed the need for a digital platform that can connect household consumers with verified service professionals. Therefore, features such as service categorization, location-based map discovery, notifications, booking status tracking, in-app messaging, and administrative verification badges were identified as essential system components.
  </p>
  <div class="page-footer">7</div>

  <br class="page-break" style="page-break-before:always;" />

  <!-- PAGE 8 -->
  <h1 class="chapter-title">Chapter 5: Conclusion and Recommendations</h1>
  
  <p>
    <span class="bold-label">Conclusion:</span><br>
    The project helped the team develop a better understanding of the problem of unorganized domestic services and the importance of structured digital coordination. The community interactions and observations showed that connecting households with verified local technicians can significantly improve convenience and trust. The study also highlighted the importance of coordination between consumers, service providers, and administrators. These findings contributed to understanding the practical requirements of the proposed <strong>ServiGo Local Services Marketplace Platform</strong>. The platform is designed to connect different stakeholders and provide facilities for service listing, booking tracking, location-based map search, notifications, and reviews.
  </p>

  <p>
    <span class="bold-label">Key Findings:</span><br>
    The study found that one of the major challenges in local services is the lack of proper communication and price transparency between customers and independent tradespeople. Timely coordination is also important because domestic emergencies (such as plumbing leaks or electrical shorts) require prompt resolution. Digital tools can support the process by providing upfront pricing, verified credentials, and real-time messaging. The findings indicate that a centralized digital platform can make service information more accessible and can improve coordination between all participants.
  </p>

  <p>
    <span class="bold-label">Recommendations:</span><br>
    Based on the findings, more awareness should be created among independent tradespeople about utilizing digital tools to expand their customer base instead of relying solely on informal word-of-mouth. Households should be encouraged to participate in organized platform bookings with transparent reviews. The proposed platform can be further improved by adding more location-based features, payment gateway integration, automated notification systems, and technician availability calendars. Future development can also focus on verification standards, safety protocols, and community engagement. Regular feedback from customers and service providers can help improve the platform and make it more useful for organizing local service economies.
  </p>
  <div class="page-footer">8</div>

  <br class="page-break" style="page-break-before:always;" />

