  <!-- PAGE 10 -->
  <h1 class="chapter-title" style="margin-bottom: 10pt;">Appendices</h1>
  
  <h2 class="section-title">Appendix A: Stakeholder Fieldwork Notes and Interview Transcripts</h2>
  <p>
    As part of the primary requirement analysis for the <strong>ServiGo Local Services Marketplace Platform</strong>, the project team conducted structured fieldwork across suburban and urban residential clusters in Mumbai. The primary objective was to capture direct insights from two key demographic groups: independent blue-collar service professionals operating in the informal market, and residential household consumers. Below are summarized transcripts of two representative interactions.
  </p>

  <p>
    <span class="bold-label">Case 1: Primary Interview with Independent Service Technician</span><br>
    <strong>Interviewee:</strong> Amit Kumar (Self-Employed Plumber, 8 Years Work Experience, Andheri East, Mumbai)<br>
    <strong>Q1. How do you currently obtain new customer leads, and what operational challenges do you experience?</strong><br>
    <em>Response:</em> "I rely almost entirely on neighborhood hardware shops referring my phone number, or past customers calling me directly. Some weeks I receive four to five jobs in a day, while in other weeks I sit idle for two to three days without any work. When I go to new clients, negotiations are always stressful because they argue about labor charges after I finish the repair."<br>
    <strong>Q2. How would an online platform like ServiGo assist your daily business operations?</strong><br>
    <em>Response:</em> "Having a verified profile with my fixed pricing and reviews would eliminate bargaining. A mobile web dashboard showing incoming booking requests with exact customer addresses, dates, and direct chat would help me plan my travel route and avoid wasting time."
  </p>

  <p>
    <span class="bold-label">Case 2: Primary Interview with Household Consumer</span><br>
    <strong>Interviewee:</strong> Rahul Sharma (Residential Apartment Owner &amp; IT Professional, Mumbai)<br>
    <strong>Q1. What major difficulties do you encounter when hiring local domestic technicians?</strong><br>
    <em>Response:</em> "Whenever we experience an electrical short-circuit or plumbing leak, finding an available technician quickly is chaotic. Local handymen quote arbitrary prices on the spot, show up hours late, and there is no guarantee of work quality. More importantly, letting completely unknown, unverified strangers into our home creates safety concerns for my family."<br>
    <strong>Q2. What features would give you the most confidence when booking a technician online?</strong><br>
    <em>Response:</em> "Administrative verification badges confirming background checks, transparent hourly and fixed rates, an interactive map showing how close the provider is, and genuine 1 to 5 star ratings from neighbors in my locality."
  </p>
  <div class="page-footer">10</div>

  <br class="page-break" style="page-break-before:always;" />

  <!-- PAGE 11 -->
  <h2 class="section-title">Fieldwork Survey Quantitative Summary</h2>
  <p>
    A localized survey conducted across 45 residential households revealed the following critical data points regarding informal home services:
  </p>
  <table class="report-table" style="font-size: 9.5pt; margin-top: 10pt;">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 45%;">Survey Inquiry Metric</th>
        <th style="width: 18%;">Affirmative (%)</th>
        <th style="width: 37%;">Key Stakeholder Concern</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Experienced arbitrary pricing / unexpected cost surges</strong></td>
        <td style="text-align: center;">84.4%</td>
        <td>Lack of standardized upfront pricing catalogs</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Encountered technician delays exceeding 2 hours</strong></td>
        <td style="text-align: center;">77.8%</td>
        <td>Absence of scheduled appointment tracking</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Expressed safety concerns hiring unverified technicians</strong></td>
        <td style="text-align: center;">88.9%</td>
        <td>Absence of formal identity verification badges</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Strongly prefer on-demand web booking with reviews &amp; map</strong></td>
        <td style="text-align: center;">93.3%</td>
        <td>High demand for transparent platforms like ServiGo</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top: 18pt;">Key Survey Insights and Takeaways</h2>
  <p>
    The quantitative findings clearly demonstrate that consumer dissatisfaction in the home service market is driven by pricing unpredictability and safety concerns. The vast majority (93.3%) of participants showed an eager willingness to migrate to a centralized digital solution that provides verified credentials, upfront service costs, and community reviews.
  </p>
  <p>
    Independent technicians likewise demonstrated a strong preference for a digital booking interface that eliminates unpaid travel and awkward post-job bargaining. These field findings validate the core architectural priorities implemented in the ServiGo application.
  </p>
  <div class="page-footer">11</div>

  <br class="page-break" style="page-break-before:always;" />

  <!-- PAGE 12 -->
  <h2 class="section-title">Appendix B: Technical Specifications, API Contracts and System Data Dictionaries</h2>
  <p>
    This appendix provides technical artefacts, core API communication contracts, and relational schema details supporting the architectural implementation of the <strong>ServiGo</strong> platform.
  </p>

  <h2 class="section-title">B.1 Core RESTful API Endpoint Payloads</h2>
  <p>
    The platform communicates via stateless RESTful endpoints utilizing JSON payloads and Bearer JWT authentication tokens:
  </p>

  <div class="code-box"><strong>// 1. Create Service Booking (POST /api/bookings)</strong>
Header: Authorization: Bearer &lt;jwt-token&gt;
Request Body:
{
  "serviceId": 3,
  "bookingDate": "2026-10-15T10:30:00.000Z",
  "address": "Flat 402, Green Valley Apts, Andheri East, Mumbai",
  "notes": "Main kitchen faucet leaking continuously."
}
Response (201 Created):
{
  "booking": {
    "id": 104,
    "customerId": 12,
    "serviceId": 3,
    "status": "pending",
    "totalAmount": 450.00,
    "createdAt": "2026-10-06T08:30:00.000Z"
  }
}</div>

  <div class="code-box"><strong>// 2. Update Booking Status (PATCH /api/bookings/104/status)</strong>
Header: Authorization: Bearer &lt;jwt-token&gt;
Request Body: { "status": "accepted" } // Allowed: pending | accepted | completed | cancelled
Response (200 OK): { "message": "Booking status updated successfully", "status": "accepted" }</div>

  <h2 class="section-title">B.2 Relational Database Schema Model Dictionary</h2>
  <table class="report-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 18%;">Model</th>
        <th style="width: 16%;">Primary Key</th>
        <th style="width: 34%;">Core Attributes &amp; Foreign Keys</th>
        <th style="width: 32%;">Relationships &amp; Constraints</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>User</strong></td>
        <td>id (Int, PK)</td>
        <td>email, password (hashed), name, phone, role</td>
        <td>1:1 with ProviderProfile; 1:N Bookings &amp; Reviews</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>ProviderProfile</strong></td>
        <td>id (Int, PK)</td>
        <td>userId (FK), businessName, experience, hourlyRate, city, isVerified</td>
        <td>References User (onDelete: Cascade); 1:N Services</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Category</strong></td>
        <td>id (Int, PK)</td>
        <td>name (Unique), description, icon</td>
        <td>1:N with Service listings</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Service</strong></td>
        <td>id (Int, PK)</td>
        <td>providerId (FK), categoryId (FK), title, price</td>
        <td>References ProviderProfile &amp; Category; 1:N Bookings</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Booking</strong></td>
        <td>id (Int, PK)</td>
        <td>customerId (FK), serviceId (FK), bookingDate, address, status, totalAmount</td>
        <td>References User &amp; Service (onDelete: Cascade)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="page-footer">12</div>

  <br class="page-break" style="page-break-before:always;" />

  <!-- PAGE 13 -->
  <h2 class="section-title">B.2 Relational Database Schema Model Dictionary (Continued)</h2>
  <table class="report-table">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th style="width: 18%;">Model</th>
        <th style="width: 16%;">Primary Key</th>
        <th style="width: 34%;">Core Attributes &amp; Foreign Keys</th>
        <th style="width: 32%;">Relationships &amp; Constraints</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Review</strong></td>
        <td>id (Int, PK)</td>
        <td>customerId (FK), providerId (FK), rating (1-5), comment</td>
        <td>References User &amp; ProviderProfile</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Conversation</strong></td>
        <td>id (Int, PK)</td>
        <td>customerId (FK), providerId (FK), lastMessage</td>
        <td>Unique composite key [customerId, providerId]</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Message</strong></td>
        <td>id (Int, PK)</td>
        <td>conversationId (FK), senderId (FK), content, read</td>
        <td>References Conversation &amp; User (onDelete: Cascade)</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top: 18pt;">B.3 Administrator Trust &amp; Verification Protocol</h2>
  <p>
    To ensure platform credibility and consumer safety, the administrative module enforces a rigorous four-stage verification protocol before granting the verified provider trust badge:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Identity Verification:</strong> Submission and validation of government-issued identity credentials (such as Aadhaar or PAN card) to establish authentic legal identity.</li>
    <li><strong>Trade Experience Audit:</strong> Verification of vocational trade diplomas, apprenticeships, or formal confirmation of declared years of field experience in plumbing, electrical, or carpentry trades.</li>
    <li><strong>Operational Phone Authentication:</strong> Direct verification and telephonic confirmation of active contact details to ensure customer reachability during scheduled visits.</li>
    <li><strong>Quality Rating Threshold Review:</strong> Continuous probationary monitoring requiring newly onboarded providers to maintain an average customer review rating of at least 4.0 out of 5 stars across initial bookings.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    Providers failing to meet verification standards remain categorized as unverified, while verified service professionals receive the blue trust badge displayed prominently across category search lists and interactive map markers.
  </p>
  <div class="page-footer">13</div>

</div>
</body>
</html>
